    pr_ref:  # 1b27
    description: "hypergumbo_core.prose_only._machine_comments matches directives (# pragma, # covers:, # noqa ...) by regex over raw lines and compares them as a sorted list. Two consequences, measured 2026-11-12 with classify():\n(1) unsafe: moving a real `# pragma: no cover` from one line to another classifies as `comments` (prose-only), so CI exempts the file from the changed-file coverage gate while coverage exclusion moved; the twice-daily full suite catches it only after merge.\n(2) safe but costly: a directive quoted inside a docstring counts, and the match runs to end of line, so rewording prose after a quoted `# pragma` in a docstring classifies as `code` (cost: a history line in a Scala test had to stay; slower import-graph selection).\nFix: take directives from real COMMENT tokens (tokenize) and key each to the code on its line."  # 1b27
    fields: {}  # 1b27
